  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Greenhouse effect, a warming of Earth&#39;s surface and troposphere (the lowest layer of the atmosphere) caused by the presence of&nbsp;water vapour, carbon dioxide, methane, and certain other gases in the air. Of those gases, known as greenhouse gases, water vapour has the largest effect.</p><p>The green house gases are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi>vapour</mi></mfenced></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>.</p>",
